# Environment template — copy to .run/env (serve.sh reads + maintains that
# path; deploy/systemd.service reads it through EnvironmentFile). KEY=VALUE,
# one per line, no quotes and no `export`. .run/ is gitignored, so this
# template is the only copy that lives in the repo.

# Public origin. One switch turns on three things at once:
#   * GET /sitemap.xml      (without SITE_URL the route 404s)
#   * robots.txt's Sitemap line
#   * absolute canonical / og:* / twitter:* URLs on every /story?id= page
# serve.sh falls back to the value below when neither the shell nor .run/env
# sets one, so a fresh clone still gets a sitemap. Use https and no trailing
# slash — the app strips it, but the crawler tags are built verbatim.
SITE_URL=https://feimatrix.com

# The /api/upload gate (X-Upload-Token must equal $UPLOAD_TOKEN). Leave this
# commented out: serve.sh generates a random token on first start and persists
# it, mode 600, in the gitignored .run/upload_token next to this file. An
# uncommented empty value would set UPLOAD_TOKEN="" and main.py refuses to
# start with an open upload route.
# UPLOAD_TOKEN=

# Where the embedding service lives (app/embeddings.py). Only semantic search,
# /api/similar and /api/approve need it; browse/tags/dates/editors/keyword
# search work without it. Point it at the big box over ssh when the deploy
# machine is too small to host llama-server.
# EMBED_URL=http://localhost:8023

# Which https hosts /api/images/{id} may 307-redirect to when a record has no
# local .webp. Keep it tight — the route must not become an open redirect for
# dataset-controlled URLs.
# IMAGE_REMOTE_HOSTS=feimatrix.com
